[h1]Custom Flags: your own images, emblems and colours for Stellaris[/h1]

Make your empire's flag truly yours. This mod upgrades the flag editor and adds example emblems and backgrounds, and the free [b]Custom Flags app[/b] lets you use your own pictures as flags, pick any colour, and design your own emblems and backgrounds. No modding experience needed.

[h2]Quick start (just this mod)[/h2]
[olist]
[*][b]Subscribe[/b], then add this mod to your playset in the Paradox launcher.
[*]In game, open the flag editor. The example emblems are under [b]Custom[/b], and the example backgrounds are at the end of the background list.
[/olist]

[h2]Use your own images and colours (free app)[/h2]
[olist]
[*][b]Download the app[/b] for Windows or Linux: [url=https://github.com/idiotgamster420/stellaris-custom-flags/releases/latest]github.com/idiotgamster420/stellaris-custom-flags[/url]
[list]
[*][b]Windows 10/11:[/b] run [i]StellarisFlagUploader-Setup.exe[/i]. If Windows says "Windows protected your PC", click [b]More info[/b], then [b]Run anyway[/b]. (The installer isn't code-signed; that costs money every year.)
[*][b]Linux:[/b] make [i]Stellaris_Flag_Uploader-x86_64.AppImage[/i] executable (right-click → Properties → Allow executing file as program) and open it.
[/list]
[*][b]Open the app once.[/b] It creates a local mod, also called [b]Custom Flags[/b], in your Stellaris mod folder. That's where your own creations go.
[*][b]Restart the Paradox launcher[/b] and add that [b]Custom Flags[/b] mod to your playset as well. Keep this Workshop mod enabled too.
[*]In the app, [b]upload images[/b], make [b]colours[/b], or design [b]backgrounds[/b] and [b]emblems[/b].
[*][b]Restart Stellaris[/b] (it only loads flags when it starts), then pick your emblem under [b]Custom[/b] in the flag editor.
[/olist]

[h2]What the app can do[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Upload any image[/b] (PNG, JPG, WebP...) as an emblem, or as the whole flag, cut neatly to the hexagon.
[*][b]Any colour[/b] for flags, map borders and ships: colour picker, hex codes, or an eyedropper that takes colours from anywhere on screen.
[*][b]Flag background and emblem maker[/b] with layers, like Black Ops 2's emblem editor.
[*][b]Flag designer[/b] that shows your flag exactly as Stellaris draws it, and tells you what to pick in game.
[/list]

[h2]Troubleshooting[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]No "Custom" category in the flag editor?[/b] Check the mods are in your [i]active[/i] playset (the launcher sometimes switches playsets off), then restart the game.
[*][b]Your changes don't show up?[/b] Restart Stellaris after changing anything in the app.
[*][b]Your own images or colours are missing?[/b] They live in the app's local [b]Custom Flags[/b] mod, so that one has to be enabled too.
[*][b]After a Stellaris update,[/b] open the app once. It rebuilds its files for the new version.
[/list]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*]Graphics and interface only. It doesn't change the game's checksum, so it's fine for multiplayer and shouldn't affect achievements.
[*]This Workshop mod works alongside UI Overhaul Dynamic. Custom colours made with the app replace the flag editor and ship colour windows, so with UI Overhaul Dynamic those two windows use the vanilla layout.
[*]In multiplayer, other players only see images made with the app if they have them too.
[/list]

[i]Not affiliated with or endorsed by Paradox Interactive.[/i]
